  {
   "id": "11",
   "dir": "11-security",
   "title": "Manage security: SELinux, firewalld, umask, SSH keys",
   "runtime": "vm",
   "tasks": "# Lab 11: Manage security\n\n1. **SELinux mode.** Put SELinux in **enforcing** mode now and at every boot.\n2. **Contexts.** Write the SELinux **type** of the running `sshd` process into `/root/sshd-type.txt` and the type of\n   `/etc/shadow` into `/root/shadow-type.txt` (just the type, e.g. `foo_t`).\n3. **Non-standard web content + port.** httpd is configured to serve `/srv/www` on **port 82**\n   (`/etc/httpd/conf.d/lab11.conf`). With SELinux enforcing, it breaks. Make it work **the SELinux way**\n   (don't disable SELinux, don't use `chcon`): a persistent file-context rule for `/srv/www`, a port label,\n   then restart httpd. `curl http://localhost:82/` must work and httpd must be enabled at boot.\n4. **Restore default contexts.** `curl http://localhost/moved.html` returns 403. Fix it.\n5. **Booleans.** Allow httpd to serve users' home directories (`httpd_enable_homedirs`), persistently.\n6. **Firewall** (default zone, permanent and active now):\n   - allow service **http** and port **82/tcp**\n   - remove the **cockpit** service\n   - **reject** all traffic from **192.168.50.99** with a rich rule\n7. **Default permissions.** User `student` must get a umask of **027** at every login\n   (new files 640, new directories 750).\n8. **SSH keys.** Set up **key-based** SSH so `student` can log in to `sally@localhost` without a password\n   (sally's password is `sally-pass`). Keep sally's `~/.ssh` permissions correct.\n",
   "solution": "# Lab 11 solution\n\n```bash\n# 1\nsetenforce 1\nsed -i 's/^SELINUX=.*/SELINUX=enforcing/' /etc/selinux/config\ngetenforce\n# 2  -Z works on ps, ls, id, cp, mkdir ...\nps -eZ | grep sshd               # system_u:system_r:sshd_t:s0-s0:c0.c1023 ...\necho sshd_t > /root/sshd-type.txt\nls -Z /etc/shadow\necho shadow_t > /root/shadow-type.txt\n# 3\nsystemctl restart httpd          # fails: \"Permission denied: could not bind to address [::]:82\"\njournalctl -t setroubleshoot -e  # or: ausearch -m AVC -ts recent ; sealert -a /var/log/audit/audit.log\nsemanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp 82\nsemanage fcontext -a -t httpd_sys_content_t '/srv/www(/.*)?'\nrestorecon -Rv /srv/www\nsystemctl enable --now httpd; systemctl restart httpd\ncurl http://localhost:82/\n# 4  mv keeps the source label (admin_home_t); cp would have taken the destination's\nls -Z /var/www/html/moved.html\nrestorecon -v /var/www/html/moved.html\n# 5\ngetsebool -a | grep homedirs\nsetsebool -P httpd_enable_homedirs on\n# 6\nfirewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=http\nfirewall-cmd --permanent --add-port=82/tcp\nfirewall-cmd --permanent --remove-service=cockpit\nfirewall-cmd --permanent --add-rich-rule='rule family=\"ipv4\" source address=\"192.168.50.99\" reject'\nfirewall-cmd --reload\nfirewall-cmd --list-all\n# 7\necho 'umask 027' >> /home/student/.bashrc\n# 8  (ssh-copy-id asks for sally's password once)\nsu - student -c 'ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -N \"\" -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519'\nsu - student -c 'ssh-copy-id sally@localhost'\nsu - student -c 'ssh sally@localhost hostname'\n```\n\n**Notes.** Never answer an SELinux task with `setenforce 0` or `chcon` on the exam: `chcon` labels don't survive a\nrelabel or `restorecon`. The pattern is always *diagnose* (`ausearch -m AVC`, `sealert`, `journalctl`), then\n*fix the policy* (`semanage fcontext` + `restorecon`, `semanage port`, `setsebool -P`). `semanage ... -l -C`\nlists only your local customizations. `man semanage-fcontext` has examples, and installing `selinux-policy-doc`\ngives per-service pages like `man httpd_selinux`. System-wide umask lives in `/etc/login.defs` (UMASK) and\n`/etc/profile.d/*.sh`; per user, in `~/.bashrc` or `~/.bash_profile`.\n",
   "files": {
    "setup.sh": "#!/bin/bash\nset -e\n. /opt/labkit/lib/vm.sh\nfor u in student sally; do id $u &>/dev/null || useradd -m $u; echo \"$u:$u-pass\" | chpasswd; done\nrm -rf /home/student/.ssh /home/sally/.ssh\nsed -i '/^umask/d' /home/student/.bashrc /home/student/.bash_profile 2>/dev/null || true\n# SELinux starts permissive (runtime and config)\nsetenforce 0 || true\nsed -i 's/^SELINUX=.*/SELINUX=permissive/' /etc/selinux/config\nsetsebool -P httpd_enable_homedirs off\n# Web content in a non-standard place, served on a non-standard port\nmkdir -p /srv/www\necho '<h1>lab11 port 82</h1>' > /srv/www/index.html\nchcon -R -t default_t /srv/www\nsemanage fcontext -d '/srv/www(/.*)?' 2>/dev/null || true\nsemanage port -d -t http_port_t -p tcp 82 2>/dev/null || true\ncat > /etc/httpd/conf.d/lab11.conf <<'C'\nListen 82\n<VirtualHost *:82>\n    DocumentRoot /srv/www\n</VirtualHost>\n<Directory /srv/www>\n    Require all granted\n</Directory>\nC\n# A file that was moved (not copied) into the web root keeps the wrong label\necho '<h1>moved page</h1>' > /root/moved.html\nmv -f /root/moved.html /var/www/html/moved.html\nchmod 644 /var/www/html/moved.html\nsystemctl enable httpd >/dev/null\nsystemctl restart httpd     # works only because SELinux is permissive right now\n# Firewall starting point\nsystemctl enable --now firewalld >/dev/null\nfirewall-cmd -q --permanent --add-service=cockpit 2>/dev/null || true\nfor s in http; do firewall-cmd -q --permanent --remove-service=$s 2>/dev/null || true; done\nfirewall-cmd -q --permanent --remove-port=82/tcp 2>/dev/null || true\nfirewall-cmd -q --permanent --remove-rich-rule='rule family=\"ipv4\" source address=\"192.168.50.99\" reject' 2>/dev/null || true\nfirewall-cmd -q --reload\n# sshd must allow passwords for the first ssh-copy-id\nsed -i 's/^#\\?PasswordAuthentication.*/PasswordAuthentication yes/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\nrm -f /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/*-cloud*.conf 2>/dev/null || true\nsystemctl restart sshd\n",
    "check.sh": "#!/bin/bash\n. /opt/labkit/lib/check.sh\nsection \"Task 1: enforcing\"\ncheck \"getenforce = Enforcing\" '[ \"$(getenforce)\" = Enforcing ]'\ncheck \"/etc/selinux/config SELINUX=enforcing\" 'grep -qx \"SELINUX=enforcing\" /etc/selinux/config'\nsection \"Task 2: contexts\"\ncheck \"sshd-type.txt = sshd_t\" '[ \"$(tr -d \"[:space:]\" < /root/sshd-type.txt)\" = sshd_t ]'\ncheck \"shadow-type.txt = shadow_t\" '[ \"$(tr -d \"[:space:]\" < /root/shadow-type.txt)\" = shadow_t ]'\nsection \"Task 3: /srv/www on port 82\"\ncheck \"persistent fcontext rule for /srv/www\" 'semanage fcontext -l -C | grep -E \"^/srv/www(\\(/\\.\\*\\)\\?)?\\s\" | grep -q httpd_sys_content_t'\ncheck \"/srv/www/index.html labelled httpd_sys_content_t\" 'ls -Z /srv/www/index.html | grep -q httpd_sys_content_t'\ncheck \"port 82/tcp labelled http_port_t\" 'semanage port -l -C | grep -E \"^http_port_t\\s+tcp\" | grep -qw 82'\ncheck \"httpd active and enabled\" 'systemctl is-active httpd && systemctl is-enabled httpd'\ncheck \"curl localhost:82 works\" 'curl -s --max-time 3 http://localhost:82/ | grep -q \"lab11 port 82\"'\nsection \"Task 4: restorecon\"\ncheck \"moved.html has httpd_sys_content_t\" 'ls -Z /var/www/html/moved.html | grep -q httpd_sys_content_t'\ncheck \"curl moved.html works\" 'curl -s --max-time 3 http://localhost/moved.html | grep -q \"moved page\"'\nsection \"Task 5: boolean\"\ncheck \"httpd_enable_homedirs on (runtime)\" 'getsebool httpd_enable_homedirs | grep -q \"on$\"'\ncheck \"httpd_enable_homedirs on (persistent)\" 'semanage boolean -l -C | grep -E \"^httpd_enable_homedirs\" | grep -q \"(on\\s*,\\s*on)\"'\nsection \"Task 6: firewall\"\nz=$(firewall-cmd --get-default-zone 2>/dev/null)\nfor mode in \"--permanent\" \"\"; do\n  label=${mode:+permanent}; label=${label:-runtime}\n  check \"http allowed ($label)\" \"firewall-cmd $mode --zone=$z --list-services | grep -qw http\"\n  check \"82/tcp allowed ($label)\" \"firewall-cmd $mode --zone=$z --list-ports | grep -qw 82/tcp\"\n  check \"cockpit removed ($label)\" \"! firewall-cmd $mode --zone=$z --list-services | grep -qw cockpit\"\n  check \"rich rule rejects 192.168.50.99 ($label)\" \"firewall-cmd $mode --zone=$z --list-rich-rules | grep 192.168.50.99 | grep -q reject\"\ndone\nsection \"Task 7: umask\"\ncheck \"student login umask is 0027\" '[ \"$(su - student -c umask)\" = 0027 ]'\nsection \"Task 8: SSH keys\"\ncheck \"student -> sally@localhost works without password\" 'su - student -c \"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new sally@localhost true\"'\ncheck \"sally ~/.ssh is 700 and authorized_keys 600\" '[ \"$(stat -c %a /home/sally/.ssh)\" = 700 ] && [ \"$(stat -c %a /home/sally/.ssh/authorized_keys)\" = 600 ]'\nsummary\n",
    "lab.conf": "TITLE=\"Manage security: SELinux, firewalld, umask, SSH keys\"\nRUNTIME=vm\n"
   }
  }
